### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- description: Detect new Bear notes tagged #share, extract core content into JSON Canvas knowledge nodes, preview via BlueBubbles iMessage, and maintain sync state. Use when setting up or running automated note-to-canvas-to-iMessage distribution pipelines, or when the user mentions "Bear share sync", "note distribution", or "share tag automation".
- Automated pipeline: Bear `#share` tag → JSON Canvas node → BlueBubbles preview.
- - **Bear** running on macOS with `grizzly` CLI installed
- - **BlueBubbles** channel configured in OpenClaw gateway
- ## Pipeline Steps
- ### 1. Detect new #share notes
- scripts/sync_share_notes.sh
- The script:
- - Polls Bear for `#share`-tagged notes via `grizzly open-tag`
- - Compares against state file (`/tmp/bear-share-sync-state.json`) to find new entries
- - Outputs `NO_NEW_NOTES` or `FOUND_NEW_NOTES:<count>`
- ### 2. Canvas update
- When new notes are found, the script automatically appends `text` nodes (color `5` = cyan) to the canvas file specified by `CANVAS_FILE` (default: `agent_capabilities.canvas`). Each node contains the note title and a 120-char content preview.
- Override the canvas path:
- CANVAS_FILE=/path/to/my.canvas scripts/sync_share_notes.sh
- ### 3. BlueBubbles notification
- After the script completes with `FOUND_NEW_NOTES`, send a preview via the `message` tool:
-   "target": "+15551234567",
-   "message": "📝 New shared note: <title>\n<content preview>"
- Read new note data from `/tmp/bear-share-new-notes.json` to get titles and content for the message.
- ### 4. Schedule recurring sync
- Use OpenClaw cron to run the pipeline on a schedule:
- cron add — schedule: every 15m — payload: "Run bear-share-sync pipeline"
- In the cron handler:
- 1. Run `scripts/sync_share_notes.sh`
- 2. If output contains `FOUND_NEW_NOTES`, read `/tmp/bear-share-new-notes.json`
- 3. Send BlueBubbles notification for each new note
- | Variable | Default | Purpose |
- |----------|---------|---------|
- | `CANVAS_FILE` | `agent_capabilities.canvas` | Target canvas file path |
- | `STATE_FILE` | `/tmp/bear-share-sync-state.json` | Processed-note tracker |
- | `BEAR_TOKEN_FILE` | `~/.config/grizzly/token` | Bear API token |
- ## Notes
- - The state file persists processed note IDs to avoid re-syncing
- - Canvas nodes are positioned sequentially at 300px intervals
- - Content is truncated to 500 chars during extraction, 120 chars in canvas node
- - Reset state: delete `$STATE_FILE` to reprocess all #share notes
+ description: Detect new Bear notes tagged #share, extract content into JSON Canvas knowledge nodes, update agent_capabilities.canvas, and broadcast previews via BlueBubbles. Use when syncing Bear notes to canvas and group chat, or when asked to "sync shared notes", "distribute Bear notes", or "publish #share notes".
+ Sync Bear notes tagged `#share` → JSON Canvas nodes → BlueBubbles group chat.
+ - Bear running with grizzly CLI installed (`go install github.com/tylerwince/grizzly/cmd/grizzly@latest`)
+ - BlueBubbles channel configured in gateway (`channels.bluebubbles`)
+ - State file at `~/.openclaw/skills/bear-share-sync/state.json` tracks processed note IDs
+ ## Workflow
+ ### 1. Poll for new #share notes
+ grizzly open-tag --name "share" --enable-callback --json --token-file ~/.config/grizzly/token
+ ```
+ Parse the JSON response to get note list. Compare against `state.json` to find unprocessed notes.
+ ### 2. Extract note content
+ For each new note, read full content:
+ grizzly open-note --id "NOTE_ID" --enable-callback --json
+ Extract: title, body (strip `#share` tag), creation date.
+ ### 3. Update agent_capabilities.canvas
+ Read the existing canvas file, append a new text node with:
+ - `id`: `bear-<note-id>` (sanitized)
+ - `type`: `text`
+ - `text`: formatted summary (title + first 200 chars + source link)
+ - `x`: auto-positioned (max existing x + 300, or 0 if empty)
+ - `y`: auto-positioned (next row at y+200 when column exceeds 4 nodes)
+ - `width`: 260, `height`: 120
+ - `color`: `"4"` (green)
+ Add an edge from the new node to a central "Shared Notes" group node if one exists.
+ Write the updated canvas JSON back.
+ ### 4. Send preview via BlueBubbles
+ ```json
+ {
+   "target": "<GROUP_CHAT_GUID>",
+   "message": "📝 New shared note: <TITLE>\n\n<PREVIEW_TEXT>\n\n— via Bear #share"
+ }
+ ### 5. Update state
+ Append processed note ID and timestamp to `state.json`.
+ See [references/config.md](references/config.md) for configurable parameters (group chat GUID, canvas path, preview length).
+ ## State File
+ `state.json` format:
+   "processed": [
+     { "id": "NOTE_ID", "title": "Note Title", "processedAt": "2026-05-12T03:00:00Z" }
+   ]
+ ## Automation
+ Set up a cron job to run this sync periodically:
+ openclaw cron add --schedule "every 15m" --payload '{"kind":"agentTurn","message":"Run bear-share-sync: poll #share notes, update canvas, send previews"}'
+ ## Scripts
+ - [scripts/sync.sh](scripts/sync.sh) — End-to-end sync script (poll → extract → canvas → notify → state update)

